IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg08-09-application`

-- LAYER 1, regulation 26: the approval of beneficial owners, officers and managers of firms in certain professions and of sole practitioners.
-- (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.)
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- THE SHAPE.  Paragraph (1) is a prohibition with an "unless"; paragraphs (3) and (3A) are two exceptions, each worded "does not breach the
-- prohibition ... if"; paragraph (12) makes a breach a criminal offence.  Whether an offence is a "relevant offence" is paragraph (14)'s
-- pointer to Schedule 3, which another part encodes (seam S-5, asking).
-- An exception worded "does not breach ... if" answers JUST FALSE when its condition fails (Marginal readings, (a); changed 2026-11-05 on the
-- reviewer's finding: an unmet "if" is the text's no); reg 26(1) then goes on to decide on the approval alone.

§ `Regulation 26 -- Prohibitions and approvals`

-- reg 26(14).  The offences listed in Schedule 3 are relevant offences for the purposes of this regulation.
-- SEAM S-5 (asking): Schedule 3 (module mlr4) answers whether the offence is a relevant offence.
-- The paragraph says the listed offences "are" relevant; it does not say that only they are.  So an offence Schedule 3 does not list is not shown to be irrelevant.
-- src:761 | (14) The offences listed in Schedule 3 are relevant offences for the purposes of this regulation.
@ref reg 26(14) (src:761-761)
GIVEN `sch 3 the offence is a relevant offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `sch 3 the offence is a relevant offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The offences listed in Schedule 3 are relevant offences" is not closed with "only"

-- reg 26(2).  The firms and sole practitioners within this paragraph are (a) auditors, insolvency practitioners, external accountants and
-- tax advisors; (b) independent legal professionals; (c) estate agents and letting agents; (d) high value dealers; (e) art market participants.
-- src:719 | (2) The firms and sole practitioners within this paragraph are—
-- src:720 | (a) auditors, insolvency practitioners, external accountants and tax advisors;
-- src:721 | (b) independent legal professionals;
-- src:722 | (c) estate agents and letting agents;
-- src:723 | (d) high value dealers;
-- src:724 | (e) art market participants.
@ref reg 26(2) (src:719-724)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of relevant person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(2) the kind of firm or sole practitioner is within this paragraph` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `auditor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `insolvency practitioner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `external accountant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `tax adviser` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `independent legal professional` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `estate agent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `letting agent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `high value dealer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `art market participant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `credit institution` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The firms and sole practitioners within this paragraph are—" is not closed with "only" (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)
    WHEN `financial institution` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The firms and sole practitioners within this paragraph are—" is not closed with "only" (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)
    WHEN `trust or company service provider` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The firms and sole practitioners within this paragraph are—" is not closed with "only" (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)
    WHEN `casino` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The firms and sole practitioners within this paragraph are—" is not closed with "only" (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)
    WHEN `cryptoasset exchange provider` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The firms and sole practitioners within this paragraph are—" is not closed with "only" (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)
    WHEN `custodian wallet provider` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The firms and sole practitioners within this paragraph are—" is not closed with "only" (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)
    WHEN `auction platform` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The firms and sole practitioners within this paragraph are—" is not closed with "only" (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)

-- reg 26(3).  A person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1) if that person has before 26th June 2018 applied to the supervisory
-- authority for approval under paragraph (6) and that application has not yet been determined.
-- src:725 | (3) A person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1) if that person has before 26th June 2018 applied to the supervisory authority for approval under paragraph (6) and that application has not yet been determined.
@ref reg 26(3) (src:725-725)
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 26(3) the date before which the application must have been made` MEANS Date 26 6 2018

@ref reg 26(3) (src:725-725)
GIVEN `the date on which the person applied to the supervisory authority for approval under paragraph (6)` IS A DATE
      `that application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(3) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the date on which the person applied to the supervisory authority for approval under paragraph (6)`) MINUS (Day `reg 26(3) the date before which the application must have been made`) LESS THAN 0 AND `that application has not yet been determined` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1) if that person has before 26th June 2018 applied ... and that application has not yet been determined" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if"; changed 2026-11-05 on review: it answered NOTHING)

-- reg 26(3A).  A person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1) if (a) that person became a relevant firm or relevant sole
-- practitioner on 10th January 2020 by virtue of an amendment to these Regulations by the Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing
-- (Amendment) Regulations 2019; (b) that person has before 10th January 2021 applied to the supervisory authority for approval under
-- paragraph (6); and (c) that application has not yet been determined.
-- src:726 | (3A) A person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1) if—
-- src:727 | (a) that person became a relevant firm or relevant sole practitioner on 10th January 2020 by virtue of an amendment to these Regulations by the Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing (Amendment) Regulations 2019;
-- src:728 | (b) that person has before 10th January 2021 applied to the supervisory authority for approval under paragraph (6); and
-- src:729 | (c) that application has not yet been determined.
@ref reg 26(3A) (src:726-729)
GIVETH A DATE
`reg 26(3A)(a) the date on which the person must have become a relevant firm or relevant sole practitioner` MEANS Date 10 1 2020

GIVETH A DATE
`reg 26(3A)(b) the date before which the application must have been made` MEANS Date 10 1 2021

@ref reg 26(3A) (src:726-729)
GIVEN `the date on which the person became a relevant firm or relevant sole practitioner` IS A DATE
      `it did so by virtue of an amendment to these Regulations by the Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing (Amendment) Regulations 2019` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the person applied to the supervisory authority for approval under paragraph (6)` IS A DATE
      `that application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(3A) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (Day `the date on which the person became a relevant firm or relevant sole practitioner`) EQUALS (Day `reg 26(3A)(a) the date on which the person must have become a relevant firm or relevant sole practitioner`) AND `it did so by virtue of an amendment to these Regulations by the Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing (Amendment) Regulations 2019` AND (Day `the date on which the person applied to the supervisory authority for approval under paragraph (6)`) MINUS (Day `reg 26(3A)(b) the date before which the application must have been made`) LESS THAN 0 AND `that application has not yet been determined` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1) if (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ..." (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if"; changed 2026-11-05 on review: it answered NOTHING)

-- reg 26(1).  No person may be the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a firm within paragraph (2) ("a relevant firm"), or a sole
-- practitioner within paragraph (2) ("a relevant sole practitioner"), unless that person has been approved ... by the supervisory authority.
-- The function answers whether the person may hold the position.  A JUST FALSE is a breach of the prohibition (see paragraph (12)).
-- src:718 | (1) No person may be the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a firm within paragraph (2) (“a relevant firm”), or a sole practitioner within paragraph (2) (“a relevant sole practitioner”), unless that person has been approved as a beneficial owner, officer or manager of the firm or as a sole practitioner by the supervisory authority of the firm or sole practitioner.
@ref reg 26(1) (src:718-718)
GIVEN `the person is the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a firm, or a sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 26(2) the kind of firm or sole practitioner is within this paragraph` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has been approved as a beneficial owner, officer or manager of the firm or as a sole practitioner by the supervisory authority of the firm or sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 26(3) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `reg 26(3A) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(1) the person may be the beneficial owner, officer or manager of the relevant firm, or the relevant sole practitioner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a firm, or a sole practitioner`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition speaks of "the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a firm within paragraph (2)" and of "a sole practitioner within paragraph (2)"
        IF `reg 26(2) the kind of firm or sole practitioner is within this paragraph` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): whether the firm or sole practitioner is within paragraph (2) is not shown
        IF `the person has been approved as a beneficial owner, officer or manager of the firm or as a sole practitioner by the supervisory authority of the firm or sole practitioner` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 26(3) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `reg 26(3A) the person does not breach the prohibition in paragraph (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person may be the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a firm within paragraph (2) ... unless that person has been approved"

DECLARE `reg 26 party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 26 the person`

DECLARE `reg 26 act` IS ONE OF
    `reg 26(1) be the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a relevant firm, or act as a relevant sole practitioner, without approval`
    `reg 26(10)(a) inform the supervisory authority which approved P of the conviction`
    `reg 26(10)(b) inform the firm's supervisory authority of P's conviction`

-- The same prohibition as a regulative rule (ruling N2: the SHANT is derived from the flat negative "No person may ... unless").  It has no
-- time limit: the text gives none, and none is invented.  An act is a breach; with no act the prohibition stands.
`reg 26(1) the prohibition on holding the position without approval` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 26 the person`
    SHANT `reg 26(1) be the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a relevant firm, or act as a relevant sole practitioner, without approval`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 26 the person` BECAUSE "the person held the position of beneficial owner, officer or manager of a relevant firm, or acted as a relevant sole practitioner, without approval"

#TRACE `reg 26(1) the prohibition on holding the position without approval` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 26 the person` DOES `reg 26(1) be the beneficial owner, officer or manager of a relevant firm, or act as a relevant sole practitioner, without approval` AT 5

#TRACE `reg 26(1) the prohibition on holding the position without approval` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- reg 26(4).  A relevant firm must take reasonable care to ensure that no-one is appointed, or continues to act, as an officer or manager
-- of the firm unless (a) that person has been approved by the supervisory authority and the approval has not ceased to be valid; or (b) that
-- person has applied for approval under paragraph (6) and the application has not yet been determined.
-- src:730 | (4) A relevant firm must take reasonable care to ensure that no-one is appointed, or continues to act, as an officer or manager of the firm unless—
-- src:731 | (a) that person has been approved by the supervisory authority, and the supervisory authority's approval of that person has not ceased to be valid; or
-- src:732 | (b) that person has applied for approval of the supervisory authority under paragraph (6) and the application has not yet been determined.
@ref reg 26(4) (src:730-732)
GIVEN `that person has been approved by the supervisory authority, and the approval has not ceased to be valid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person has applied for approval under paragraph (6) and the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(4) the person may be appointed, or continue to act, as an officer or manager of the relevant firm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `that person has been approved by the supervisory authority, and the approval has not ceased to be valid` OR `that person has applied for approval under paragraph (6) and the application has not yet been determined` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no-one is appointed, or continues to act, as an officer or manager of the firm unless— (a) ...; or (b) ..."

@ref reg 26(4) (src:730-732)
GIVEN `it has taken reasonable care to ensure that no-one is appointed, or continues to act, as an officer or manager of the firm unless approved or awaiting a determination of an application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(4) the relevant firm has taken reasonable care as paragraph (4) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken reasonable care to ensure that no-one is appointed, or continues to act, as an officer or manager of the firm unless approved or awaiting a determination of an application` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant firm must take reasonable care to ensure" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 26(5).  A relevant sole practitioner must not act, or continue to act, as a sole practitioner unless (a) approved by the supervisory
-- authority and the approval has not ceased to be valid; or (b) applied for approval under paragraph (6) and not yet determined.
-- src:733 | (5) A relevant sole practitioner must not act, or continue to act, as a sole practitioner unless—
-- src:734 | (a) that person has been approved by the supervisory authority, and the supervisory authority's approval of that person has not ceased to be valid; or
-- src:735 | (b) that person has applied for approval of the supervisory authority under paragraph (6) and the application has not yet been determined.
@ref reg 26(5) (src:733-735)
GIVEN `that person has been approved by the supervisory authority, and the approval has not ceased to be valid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person has applied for approval under paragraph (6) and the application has not yet been determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(5) the relevant sole practitioner may act, or continue to act, as a sole practitioner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `that person has been approved by the supervisory authority, and the approval has not ceased to be valid` OR `that person has applied for approval under paragraph (6) and the application has not yet been determined` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant sole practitioner must not act, or continue to act, as a sole practitioner unless— (a) ...; or (b) ..."

-- reg 26(6).  An application for the approval of the supervisory authority under paragraph (1) may be made by or on behalf of the person concerned.
-- src:736 | (6) An application for the approval of the supervisory authority under paragraph (1) may be made by or on behalf of the person concerned.
@ref reg 26(6) (src:736-736)
GIVEN `the application is made by the person concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made on behalf of the person concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(6) the application may be made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is made by the person concerned` OR `the application is made on behalf of the person concerned` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the application "may be made by or on behalf of the person concerned"; the paragraph says nothing of an application made by anyone else

-- reg 26(7).  The application must (a) be made in such manner as the supervisory authority may direct; (b) contain, or be accompanied by
-- (i) sufficient information to enable the supervisory authority, if it is a self-regulatory organisation, to determine whether the person
-- concerned has been convicted of a relevant offence; and (ii) such other information as the supervisory authority may reasonably require.
-- src:737 | (7) The application must—
-- src:738 | (a) be made in such manner as the supervisory authority may direct;
-- src:739 | (b) contain, or be accompanied by—
-- src:740 | (i) sufficient information to enable the supervisory authority, if it is a self-regulatory organisation, to determine whether the person concerned has been convicted of a relevant offence; and
-- src:741 | (ii) such other information as the supervisory authority may reasonably require.
@ref reg 26(7) (src:737-741)
GIVEN `the application is made in such manner as the supervisory authority may direct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains, or is accompanied by, sufficient information to enable the supervisory authority, if it is a self-regulatory organisation, to determine whether the person concerned has been convicted of a relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains, or is accompanied by, such other information as the supervisory authority may reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(7) the application is made as paragraph (7) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the application is made in such manner as the supervisory authority may direct` AND `the application contains, or is accompanied by, sufficient information to enable the supervisory authority, if it is a self-regulatory organisation, to determine whether the person concerned has been convicted of a relevant offence` AND `the application contains, or is accompanied by, such other information as the supervisory authority may reasonably require` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- SEAM S-11 (answering): regulation 46(1)(b) (module mlr3) takes the answer to whether the application meets the requirements of regulation 26(7).
@ref reg 26(7) (src:737-741)
GIVEN `the application is made in such manner as the supervisory authority may direct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains, or is accompanied by, sufficient information to enable the supervisory authority, if it is a self-regulatory organisation, to determine whether the person concerned has been convicted of a relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains, or is accompanied by, such other information as the supervisory authority may reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(7) the application for approval meets the requirements of regulation 26(7)` MEANS
    `reg 26(7) the application is made as paragraph (7) requires` `the application is made in such manner as the supervisory authority may direct` `the application contains, or is accompanied by, sufficient information to enable the supervisory authority, if it is a self-regulatory organisation, to determine whether the person concerned has been convicted of a relevant offence` `the application contains, or is accompanied by, such other information as the supervisory authority may reasonably require`

-- reg 26(8)(a).  The supervisory authority must grant an application for approval under paragraph (6) unless the applicant has been convicted of a relevant offence.
-- src:742 | (8) The supervisory authority—
-- src:743 | (a) must grant an application for approval under paragraph (6) unless the applicant has been convicted of a relevant offence;
-- src:744 | (b) may grant an application so as to give approval only for a limited period.
@ref reg 26(8) (src:742-744)
GIVEN `the applicant has been convicted of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(8)(a) the supervisory authority must grant the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the applicant has been convicted of an offence`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must grant an application for approval under paragraph (6) unless the applicant has been convicted of a relevant offence"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a relevant offence is Schedule 3's question and has not been answered

-- reg 26(8)(b).  The supervisory authority may grant an application so as to give approval only for a limited period.
@ref reg 26(8)(b) (src:742-744)
GIVEN `the approval is given only for a limited period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(8)(b) the supervisory authority may grant the application so as to give approval only for a limited period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the approval is given only for a limited period` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): sub-paragraph (b) says the authority "may" give a limited approval; it does not say it must give an unlimited one

-- reg 26(9).  An approval given under paragraph (8) (a) is not valid if the approved person has been convicted of a relevant offence; (b) ceases
-- to be valid if the approved person is subsequently convicted of a relevant offence.
-- src:745 | (9) An approval given by a supervisory authority under paragraph (8)—
-- src:746 | (a) is not valid if the person approved under paragraph (1) (the “approved person”) has been convicted of a relevant offence;
-- src:747 | (b) ceases to be valid if the approved person is subsequently convicted of a relevant offence.
@ref reg 26(9) (src:745-747)
GIVEN `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the approved person had been convicted of the offence when the approval was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approved person is subsequently convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(9) the approval given under paragraph (8) is valid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the approved person had been convicted of the offence when the approval was given` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) is not valid if the person approved under paragraph (1) (the “approved person”) has been convicted of a relevant offence"
        IF `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the approved person is subsequently convicted of the offence` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) ceases to be valid if the approved person is subsequently convicted of a relevant offence"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (9) says when an approval is not valid or ceases to be valid; it does not say when it is valid

-- reg 26(10).  If an approved person ("P") is convicted of a relevant offence (a) P must inform the supervisory authority which approved P of the
-- conviction within 30 days of the day on which P was convicted; (b) the relevant firm for which P was approved must inform its supervisory
-- authority of the conviction within 30 days of the date on which the firm became aware of P's conviction.
-- src:748 | (10) If an approved person (“P”) is convicted of a relevant offence—
-- src:749 | (a) P must inform the supervisory authority which approved P of the conviction within 30 days of the day on which P was convicted;
-- src:750 | (b) the relevant firm for which P was approved must inform its supervisory authority of the conviction within 30 days of the date on which the firm became aware of P's conviction.
@ref reg 26(10) (src:748-750)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 26(10) the period of 30 days` MEANS 30

@ref reg 26(10)(a) (src:748-750)
GIVEN `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date on which P was convicted` IS A DATE
      `the date on which P informed the supervisory authority which approved P` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(10)(a) P informed the supervisory authority within 30 days of the conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "If an approved person (“P”) is convicted of a relevant offence" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): an "if" not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF NOT (`reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a relevant offence has not been answered
        IF (Day `the date on which P informed the supervisory authority which approved P`) MINUS (Day `the date on which P was convicted`) LESS THAN 0 THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days of the day on which P was convicted" speaks of the days after the conviction (Ruling 2026-11-05, (a): outside the period the text fixes in its own words; a date before the period begins is outside it, fork F-period)
        IF (Day `the date on which P informed the supervisory authority which approved P`) MINUS (Day `the date on which P was convicted`) AT MOST `reg 26(10) the period of 30 days` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "P must inform the supervisory authority which approved P of the conviction within 30 days of the day on which P was convicted" (Marginal readings, (c) and (d))

@ref reg 26(10)(b) (src:748-750)
GIVEN `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the firm became aware of P's conviction` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the firm informed its supervisory authority` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(10)(b) the relevant firm informed its supervisory authority within 30 days of becoming aware of the conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "If an approved person (“P”) is convicted of a relevant offence" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): an "if" not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF NOT (`reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a relevant offence has not been answered
        IF (Day `the date on which the firm informed its supervisory authority`) MINUS (Day `the date on which the firm became aware of P's conviction`) LESS THAN 0 THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days of the date on which the firm became aware" speaks of the days after it became aware (Ruling 2026-11-05, (a): outside the period the text fixes in its own words; a date before the period begins is outside it, fork F-period)
        IF (Day `the date on which the firm informed its supervisory authority`) MINUS (Day `the date on which the firm became aware of P's conviction`) AT MOST `reg 26(10) the period of 30 days` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant firm for which P was approved must inform its supervisory authority of the conviction within 30 days of the date on which the firm became aware of P's conviction" (Marginal readings, (c) and (d))

`reg 26(10)(a) the duty of P to inform the supervisory authority within 30 days of the conviction` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 26 the person`
    MUST `reg 26(10)(a) inform the supervisory authority which approved P of the conviction`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 26 the person` BECAUSE "the supervisory authority was not informed within 30 days of the day on which P was convicted"

`reg 26(10)(b) the duty of the relevant firm to inform its supervisory authority within 30 days of becoming aware` MEANS
    PARTY `reg 26 the person`
    MUST `reg 26(10)(b) inform the firm's supervisory authority of P's conviction`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `reg 26 the person` BECAUSE "the supervisory authority was not informed within 30 days of the date on which the firm became aware of P's conviction"

#TRACE `reg 26(10)(a) the duty of P to inform the supervisory authority within 30 days of the conviction` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 26 the person` DOES `reg 26(10)(a) inform the supervisory authority which approved P of the conviction` AT 30

#TRACE `reg 26(10)(a) the duty of P to inform the supervisory authority within 30 days of the conviction` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

#TRACE `reg 26(10)(b) the duty of the relevant firm to inform its supervisory authority within 30 days of becoming aware` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `reg 26 the person` DOES `reg 26(10)(b) inform the firm's supervisory authority of P's conviction` AT 30

#TRACE `reg 26(10)(b) the duty of the relevant firm to inform its supervisory authority within 30 days of becoming aware` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

-- reg 26(11).  If the beneficial owner of a relevant firm is convicted of a relevant offence, the High Court (or in Scotland the Court of
-- Session) may, on the application of the supervisory authority, order the sale of the beneficial owner's interest in that firm.
-- src:751 | (11) If the beneficial owner of a relevant firm is convicted of a relevant offence, the High Court (or in Scotland the Court of Session) may, on the application of the supervisory authority, order the sale of the beneficial owner's interest in that firm.
@ref reg 26(11) (src:751-751)
GIVEN `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the supervisory authority has applied to the High Court (or in Scotland the Court of Session)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(11) the court may order the sale of the beneficial owner's interest in the firm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 26(14) the offence is a relevant offence for the purposes of this regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the supervisory authority has applied to the High Court (or in Scotland the Court of Session)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the court "may, on the application of the supervisory authority, order the sale" where the beneficial owner "is convicted of a relevant offence"; the paragraph says nothing of other cases

-- reg 26(12).  A person who, in breach of the prohibition in paragraph (1), (a) acts as a manager or officer of a relevant firm or as a
-- relevant sole practitioner; or (b) is knowingly a beneficial owner of a relevant firm, is guilty of a criminal offence.
-- src:752 | (12) A person who, in breach of the prohibition in paragraph (1)—
-- src:753 | (a) acts as a manager or officer of a relevant firm or as a relevant sole practitioner; or
-- src:754 | (b) is knowingly a beneficial owner of a relevant firm,
-- src:755 | is guilty of a criminal offence.
@ref reg 26(12) (src:752-755)
GIVEN `reg 26(1) the person may be the beneficial owner, officer or manager of the relevant firm, or the relevant sole practitioner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person acts as a manager or officer of a relevant firm or as a relevant sole practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is knowingly a beneficial owner of a relevant firm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(12) the person is guilty of a criminal offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `reg 26(1) the person may be the beneficial owner, officer or manager of the relevant firm, or the relevant sole practitioner` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND (`the person acts as a manager or officer of a relevant firm or as a relevant sole practitioner` OR `the person is knowingly a beneficial owner of a relevant firm`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who, in breach of the prohibition in paragraph (1), (a) ...; or (b) ..., is guilty of a criminal offence"; the paragraph says nothing of a person outside it (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)

-- reg 26(13).  A person guilty of an offence under paragraph (12) is liable (a) on summary conviction (i) in England and Wales, to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both; (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term
-- not exceeding three months, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both; (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding two years, to a fine or to both.
DECLARE `reg 26(13) conviction` IS ONE OF
    `reg 26(13)(a)(i) summary conviction in England and Wales`
    `reg 26(13)(a)(ii) summary conviction in Scotland or Northern Ireland`
    `reg 26(13)(b) conviction on indictment`
    `reg 26(13) conviction elsewhere`

-- src:756 | (13) A person who is guilty of a criminal offence under paragraph (12) is liable—
-- src:757 | (a) on summary conviction—
-- src:758 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine or to both;
-- src:759 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both;
-- src:760 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, to a fine or to both.
@ref reg 26(13) (src:756-760)
GIVEN conviction IS A `reg 26(13) conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 26(13) the longest term of imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER conviction
    WHEN `reg 26(13)(a)(i) summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `reg 26(13)(a)(ii) summary conviction in Scotland or Northern Ireland` THEN JUST 3
    WHEN `reg 26(13)(b) conviction on indictment` THEN JUST 24
    WHEN `reg 26(13) conviction elsewhere` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (13) fixes the term for summary conviction in the three nations and for conviction on indictment

@ref reg 26(13) (src:756-760)
GIVEN conviction IS A `reg 26(13) conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 26(13) the fine is limited to the statutory maximum` MEANS
    CONSIDER conviction
    WHEN `reg 26(13)(a)(i) summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "a fine" with no limit stated
    WHEN `reg 26(13)(a)(ii) summary conviction in Scotland or Northern Ireland` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `reg 26(13)(b) conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "a fine" with no limit stated
    WHEN `reg 26(13) conviction elsewhere` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (13) says nothing of this conviction
